# B&B Sample Diet PDF (`b&bsamplediet.pdf`)

**Deliverable filename:** `docs/samples/b&bsamplediet.pdf` — **locked**. Overwritten each render. **Do not rename** without explicit user request.

**Pages:** Welcome → Lean Body Analysis → Food Plan → Servings → Food List (protein/grains) → Food List (vegetables/fruit) — **6 pages**.

## Pipeline

| Piece | Path |
|-------|------|
| Renderer | `server/pdf/renderSampleDietPrintout.js` |
| Payload | `js/sampleDietPrintoutData.js` → `buildSampleDietPreviewPayload()` |
| Fixtures | `js/sampleDietPreviewFixtures.js`, `js/printoutVerifyFixtures.js` |
| Copy | `js/sampleDietPrintoutCopyData.js`, `js/sampleDietAceData.js` |
| Frame | `server/pdf/draw1982Frame.js` |
| Render script | `scripts/render-sample-diet-preview.mjs` |
| Deliverable | `docs/samples/b&bsamplediet.pdf` |

Run: `npm run render:sample-diet-preview`

## Delivery order (critical)

1. Edit code
2. `npm run render:sample-diet-preview`
3. **Commit** `docs/samples/b&bsamplediet.pdf`
4. **`git push origin main`**
5. **Only then** give the download link (use script `DOWNLOAD` line)

## Give the user (one link — Safari saves to Downloads)

```
https://burnandbuilddiet.com/download/sample-diet/
```

That page redirects to the API with `Content-Disposition: attachment` so Safari saves `b&bsamplediet.pdf` instead of opening it inline.

Direct attachment URL (fallback / Terminal):

```
https://program-creator-3tzd.onrender.com/api/samples/sample-diet
```

(`npm run render:sample-diet-preview` prints `DOWNLOAD` and `ATTACHMENT` lines after push.)

If download still fails, give the script `CURL` line (Mac Terminal → `~/Downloads/b&bsamplediet.pdf`).

## What worked (locked — do not change)

User confirmed this delivery pattern on Mac Downloads (Aug 2026). **Keep doing it exactly this way:**

1. **One filename forever:** `b&bsamplediet.pdf` in `docs/samples/` — overwrite in place each render. No numbered files (`-N`, `-latest`), no renames, no second copy with a different name.
2. **One download URL forever:** paste the `DOWNLOAD` line from `npm run render:sample-diet-preview` (`https://burnandbuilddiet.com/download/sample-diet/`). Never send raw GitHub URLs or `github.com/.../blob/...` — Safari opens those inline.
3. **Push before link:** render → commit PDF → `git push origin main` → **then** paste the link. Linking early serves stale bytes; user waits on GitHub cache (~minutes).
4. **One link per update:** do not send multiple conflicting URLs in one session. Same link every time until the filename changes (which it must not, unless the user asks).
5. **Downloads clutter:** if the user re-downloads while the file already exists, macOS saves `b&bsamplediet-2.pdf` — that is normal. Tell them to keep the newest `b&bsamplediet.pdf` and delete older numbered / legacy names (`bb-five-page-sample-female-*`, etc.).

Renaming the deliverable or switching to numbered PDFs ** broke downloads** and filled Downloads with duplicate files. Do not repeat.

## Do not

| Wrong | Why |
|-------|-----|
| Rename the deliverable file | Breaks the user's working download link |
| Link before push | GitHub serves old or missing file |
| Cursor artifacts panel | Broken download UX on Cursor Web |
| Raw GitHub PDF URL | Safari opens inline; does not save to Downloads |
